  "body": "Design record for [#5973](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5973), child of the worlds programme [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955) (S75–S76). Docs only; no implementation.\n\n**Record:** [world-governance design](https://github.com/developing-today/code/blob/queue/12862-5973-world-governance/doc/2026-11-08T13-45-00Z_design_id_world_governance/2026-11-08T13-45-00Z_design_id_world_governance.md) (PR head; becomes a main-branch doc when merged).\n\n## Settled in the record\n\n- **Moderation-as-library interface (§2):** typed policy module plus platform authority adapter; platform owns transport, validation, effects, and journaling; world supplies policy.\n- **Capability and authority (§2.4–§3):** no moderation provider privilege; default capability footprint is only the bounded governance-event input. Optional context providers require explicit, audience-scoped grants. Writer-set inclusion remains view-counting only and never confers moderation authority.\n- **Per-world configuration (§4):** one library/policy configured with reviewer/moderator sets, report thresholds, and exemptions; not forks. KDL serialization stays deferred to #5753.\n- **Pre-approval (§5):** world-object artifact hash, exact requested-capability footprint, world/policy versions, and approver proof; approval grants no capability.\n- **Boards boundary (§6):** cross-pollinates merged #5861 principles but keeps board view-bans, world revocation, authority, action vocabularies, and storage separate; #5680 remains open.\n\n## Fresh relation state (2026-11-09)\n\n#5680 OPEN; #5861 CLOSED with its merged record in PR #7857; #5545 CLOSED (view-projection/discovery implementation, not moderator authority); #5753 OPEN and blocked; parent #5955 OPEN. See the record's §8 for these corrections and source drift.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796737342&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7708&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7708&signature=e8b89f1a2357893d726408ed45070be84315ce8a573f848486f5f8d0f980db62\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7708?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
